<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ogedengbe</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1822–<a href="/years/1910">1910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Ogedengbe Agbogungboro</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ogedengbe was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> war leader from Ilesa in the Ijesha kingdom of south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. Once a captive and warrior in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibadan">Ibadan</a>'s service, he became the chief commander of the Ekiti Parapo alliance against Ibadan in the Kiriji war from 1877. The war ended with a British-brokered peace in 1886, and he later held the title Obanla of Ilesa.</p></div>
